From: genshanxinli <127909456+genshanxinli@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: refuse to offload flows behind a shaping qdisc

The PPE driver hardcodes AIROHA_FOE_SHAPER_ID to 0x7f (unshaped), so
offloaded flows bypass software rate-shaping qdiscs on both egress and
ingress paths.  Checking only the final physical netdev root qdisc inside
airoha_ppe_foe_entry_prepare() misses shapers attached to upper tunnel or
VLAN devices (pppoe-wan, wan.100), mq per-TXQ subqueues, child qdiscs in
dev->qdisc_hash, and ingress redirect/police chains (sqm-scripts ifb4*,
qosify downlink ifb-wan, act_police).

Export an RCU-only helper tc_netdev_has_shaper_rcu() from net/sched/cls_api.c
that inspects:
  - the root qdisc, mq TXQ qdisc_sleeping entries, and dev->qdisc_hash
    against non-offloaded software shaping qdiscs;
  - per-block RCU-tracked police and mirred redirect actions attached to
    dev->tcx_ingress (non-recursively checking only the egress shaper of
    each mirred target, avoiding false positives on pure qosify cls_bpf or
    ifb-dns fq_codel redirects).

Reject flowtable offload in nft_dev_path_info() when any hop along the
forward path has an active shaper, and keep a defense-in-depth check on
both egress and ingress netdevs in airoha_ppe_flow_offload_replace().

Origin: archive/xr1710g-v1@e85677d284c0; local, xr1710g #424
Signed-off-by: genshanxinli <127909456+genshanxinli@users.noreply.github.com>
